.docname {Boolean}
.include {docs}

Boolean values are represented by the following literals, which are **case insensitive**:

| Boolean value | Literals      |
|---------------|---------------|
| **`true`**    | `true`, `yes` |
| **`false`**   | `false`, `no` |

Using the `yes` and `no` literals is encouraged because they contribute to a more natural language flow.

```markdown
.code linenumbers:{no}
  My code
```

## Operators

The following operator functions return a `Boolean` value. The [chaining syntax](syntax-of-a-function-call.qd#chaining-calls) is recommended (e.g. `.value::equals {other}`

- `.not {bool}`: Negates a boolean.
- `.and {a} {b}`: Returns `true` if both `a` and `b` are `true`.
- `.or {a} {b}`: Returns `true` if at least one of `a` and `b` is `true`.
- `.islower {a} {than}`: Returns `true` if `a` is less than `than`
- `.isgreater {a} {than}`: Returns `true` if `a` is greater than `than`
- `.isequal {a} {to}`: Returns `true` if `a` equals `to`
- `.contains {value} {element}`: Returns `true` if the string `value` contains the text `element`, or if the collection `value` contains `element` as an element, or if the dictionary `value` contains `element` as a key
